---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Refund Policy — CG Design & Co."
  description="When and how refunds work for CG Design & Co. websites, branding and setup jobs, including your rights under Australian and UK consumer law."
  pageTitle="Refund Policy"
  lastUpdated="20 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy sits alongside our
    <a href={`${base}/terms-and-conditions/`}>Terms &amp; Conditions</a>. It
    doesn't limit any guarantee or remedy you have under the Australian
    Consumer Law, or, if you're a UK consumer, the Consumer Rights Act 2015
    and the Consumer Contracts Regulations 2013.
  </p>

  <h2>If there's a problem with our work</h2>
  <p>
    If something we built doesn't work as agreed, tell us and we'll fix it
    at no extra cost. If there's a major failure, such as work that's
    substantially unfit for its purpose or can't be fixed in a reasonable
    time, you can choose to cancel and get a refund for the affected work,
    or to receive compensation for the drop in value.
  </p>

  <h2>Before work begins</h2>
  <p>
    If you change your mind before we've started work, any deposit you've
    paid is refunded in full.
  </p>

  <h2>UK and EU consumers: 14 days to cancel</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel within 14 days of accepting our quote, for any reason.
    If you asked us to start during those 14 days, we'll refund what you've
    paid minus a fair amount for the work done before you told us. If the
    work was fully completed at your request within the 14 days, this
    cancellation right no longer applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Once work is underway</h2>
  <p>
    If you cancel partway through, we charge only for the work actually
    completed:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your deposit covers the work done up to that point.</li>
    <li>Anything you've paid beyond that is refunded within 14 days.</li>
    <li>If the deposit doesn't cover the work completed, we'll invoice you for the difference.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Once a project is finished and paid for</h2>
  <p>
    A finished website is custom work made for your business, so we don't
    give refunds just because you've changed your mind once the final
    payment is made and the site has been handed over. This never affects
    your right to a fix, refund or compensation if our work has a problem,
    as set out above.
  </p>

  <h2>Monthly hosting &amp; care plans</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel a monthly plan at any time. You won't be charged again
    after your current month, and we don't give partial refunds for a month
    already paid, unless the service wasn't provided as agreed.
  </p>

  <h2>How refunds are paid</h2>
  <p>
    Refunds are paid in Australian dollars (AUD) to the card or account you
    paid with, within 14 days of being agreed. If you paid from outside
    Australia, the amount you receive may differ slightly because of
    exchange rates set by your bank.
  </p>

  <h2>How to ask for a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:info@cgdesignaus.com">info@cgdesignaus.com</a>
    with your name and project details, and we'll reply within a few
    working days.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
